# Keep the build context small and — more importantly — keep secrets out of it.
# Everything sent to the daemon is readable from any layer that COPYs it, so a
# `.env` that reaches the context reaches the image, and `docker history` shows
# it to anyone who can pull.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
secrets/

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

.git/
.github/

# Note what is *not* here: `app/`, `tests/`, `migrations/` and `seed/`. The
# Dockerfile copies the first and the tests are meant to be runnable against a
# built image, so excluding them would trade a slightly smaller context for a
# repository whose own test suite cannot be run the way CI would run it.
